From: Retro Receipts replay lane
Subject: [PATCH] agent — read BOTH teams at character select, locally

⚠⚠ STATUS 2026-08-26: DE-CONFLICTED, NOT APPLIED, NOT MINE TO LAND.
This patch was authored by another session (transcript 87af92a3, the original replay lane) against
`main`, and it collided with agent 0.3.24 on branch `replay-capture-0.3.24`: it declared
`MODE_OFF = 0x3cb8`, which already exists there as `BLK_MODE_OFF`, and `H_STRIDE = 0x738`, which
already exists in reader.rs as the crate-level `STRIDE`. It also called `pointer_follow_blk()`,
which does not exist in the file.

Rewritten here to apply cleanly ON TOP OF `replay-capture-0.3.24` using the constants already in
the file, so the duplicate names can never land. **The idea and the RE are the original author's;
only the naming and the missing helper are changed.** Whoever owns this area decides whether to
apply it — the replay lane has deliberately not applied it.

WHY IT WORKS (measured live 2026-08-26, docs/STEAM-GGPO-DETERMINISM.md §2b):
  * screen    : blk+0x3CB8 byte[2]  ->  1 = CHARACTER SELECT, 2 = IN BATTLE
  * selection : blk + 0x3DB8 + i*0x738 + 0x6C0   (the fighter slot's CID field)
    THE CHARACTER-SELECT CURSOR WRITES ITS SELECTION STRAIGHT INTO THE FIGHTER SLOT.
    Found by differential capture: park P1 on one character, snapshot blk, move, snapshot, diff.
    Exactly two words changed: blk+0x4478 (= blk+0x3DB8+0x6C0, slot 0 CID) went 0x3a -> 0x34,
    i.e. 58 (Servbot) -> 52 (Sentinel) — the two characters actually selected.
  * slots interleave as everywhere else: EVEN = P1 team, ODD = P2 team.
  * ⚠ 0x3DB8 is the TRUE object base. Do NOT use MATCH_ARR_ADD (0x3f24) — that is 0x16C INSIDE the
    object (see rr-steam-object-base-fix); 0x3f24 - 0x16c = 0x3db8, which is the identity below.

WHY IT MATTERS FOR MONEY MATCHES: both teams become readable the instant they lock in, locally,
BEFORE the fight starts. Team verification and wager locking stop depending on a client report.

⚠ CORRECTION to the original patch's caution: it said to treat the read as final "once the mode
flips to 2, or once the values hold steady". Use the MODE EDGE, not steadiness — the cursor writes
into the slot continuously while a player hovers, and a player who parks on a character for a
second looks identical to a locked pick. Measured live: character select runs ~500-1800 frames, so
"steady" is reached often and early.

Apply from the RetroReceipts-agent repo root, on branch replay-capture-0.3.24:
